{{also|Heathen}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang|en}} ''[[hæþen|hǣþen]]'', akin to {{m|en|heath||heathland}}. Cognate with Dutch ''[[heiden]]'', German ''[[Heide]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|iːðən|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Not adhering to an [[Abrahamic]] [[religion]]; [[pagan]].
# {{context|by extension|lang=en}} Uncultured; uncivilized; savage, [[philistine]].
# {{alternative case form of|Heathen|nodot=1|lang=en}} {{gloss|pertaining or adhering to the Germanic [[neo-pagan]] faith [[Heathenry]]}}.

